    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 14 tests across Cp01\u2013Cp07, **0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the default-registration-date behavior for `POST /api/owners`. When no `registrationDate` is supplied it's set to the server's current date, and it's returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format (a supplied date is kept as-is).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` gain a `LocalDate registrationDate` field on both the request and response sides. It's optional (not in `required`), and Jackson serializes `LocalDate` as `YYYY-MM-DD` (same as the existing `Pet.birthDate`).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `registrationDate` field (`@Column(name = \"registration_date\")`) with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it by name automatically in both directions.\n\n3. **`BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 after mapping the request to an `Owner`, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the request omitted it. This is the single build step in the POST pipeline, so a supplied date flows through untouched while an absent one gets today's date before `SaveOwner`.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 added a nullable `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table so the field persists across all profiles (hsqldb runs with `ddl-auto=none`, so the explicit column is required there).\n\nThe two new `Cp07Tests` (`coreDefaultsTotoday` and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) both pass, and no existing tests regressed.",
